997 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049997 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049997 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Integrals Over Type I Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049997 #edb/ref 1033 2151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049997 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "24e61144-3626-5d23-b2e6-a33ee94f32f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Integrals Over Rectangular Domains" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1033 1992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050207 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "36521b0a-e13c-5296-b2d4-078f2470ad6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Integrals Over Type II Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1033 2152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3ab583b8-5390-5f48-b28b-1a89db70664f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129027 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129027 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/73/73e2bd9a47c9d16f93d5240db3c4babc36f9fbe703ac9e0af449acaa7528f804.png)\n\nA triangular plate occupies the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) enclosed between the lines ![](images/1f/1fb33239355d26c5ef03e27bcf8b6a9c4c0509d9b045eb92713f0d0256d5e29f.svg) and ![](images/b5/b58ea57e60be24c13d7c381e1323204c3e923297cde1a4c0ba80f7bacf5f08dc.svg) as shown above. The plate's mass density function ![](images/98/98a445be63a324ba80515c96b7f891797392bdeafb375acb75ce1613f4475d4c.svg) is given by ![](images/8e/8e97b851d06a96a87df2aff865e5eee8cde69fa8ebb76b314ec691ecae0c6a4c.svg) Find the total mass of the triangular plate." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27249c57-7f17-5e3e-9a21-0518320f5076" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129027 #edb/ref 1074 "The mass of the triangular plate occupying the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) with mass density ![](images/ee/eeea59e41716100d371e35f6a9cb2a2bd7a9285a7b849d8eac060daa0ba4d2be.svg) is given by\n\n![](images/75/7547107cd7e0b796f759b9f61151228a65276fdf9b1ee368f31527f5e88634ee.svg)\n\nNotice that ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a type I region. So, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n![](images/e9/e92fc28ba8f4ba932b8a4596648cf1ad13b47180ee681caad1c72ede2c7fbc68.svg)\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to ![](images/f4/f4e3bd65ea5e543add33f4a03c10e6b51bba71ff45e1eee33a9ce7e01d064ac7.svg) treating ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) as a constant:\n\n![](images/0b/0bd607261ba1e95bff1b7d060d85791252208b530c096dcc2dca555f9a890b25.svg)\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to ![](images/06/06d9e6ee04f202e0e861c51f0cd11ce47727f565d64d834fa625baea04ae11e6.svg)\n\n![](images/59/59ac221987617d4c92321338b3646c155d483ede3f26614a615f6e3e49ff820f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the total mass of the plate is ![](images/c0/c06c6ac73c4cffd1c6d5f2e1a2a15e193ea80f6a97d595e2e6e9dd478261d2e6.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129028 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129028 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the total charge $Q$ of a metal plate that occupies the region $D = \\{ (x,y) : 0 \\le x \\le 1, \\, 0 \\le y \\le 2\\}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y) = 4 - 3y^2 + 2x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129028 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d565cc1a-f78f-5712-8a03-df4d4e8f3e21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129028 #edb/ref 1074 "The total charge $Q$ of a plate that occupies the region $D = \\{ (x,y) : 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\, 0 \\leq y \\leq 2\\}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y) = 4 - 3y^2 + 2x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & ={∬}_{D}(4-3{y}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} (4 - 3y^2 + 2x) \\:\\textrm{d}A\n= \\int_{0}^2 \\left[ \\int_{0}^1 (4 - 3y^2 + 2x) \\:\\textrm{d}x \\right] \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-3{y}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[4x-3{y}^{2}x+{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[(4(1)-3{y}^{2}(1)+(1)^{2})-(4(0)-3{y}^{2}(0)-(0)^{2})]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y & =[5y-{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(5(2)-(2)^{3})-(5(0)-(0)^{3}) \\\\  & =(10-8)-0 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the charge of the plate is $Q=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129029 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8195" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129029 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f0/f0db928874dba8d872cde46d1467686010f3484765b2d7e39807b5a32a131b09.png)\n\nFind the total charge $Q$ of a copper plate that occupies the region $D$ shown above, and has charge density \n\n$$\n\\rho (x,y) = \\dfrac{4x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}  .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129029 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92b9b5ea-1153-580a-a03a-94338f30fe3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129029 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the region $D$ represents one-quarter of the disk of radius $3$ centered at \n$\\left(0,0\\right).$\n\nThe total charge $Q$ of an object occupying the region $D$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y) =  \\dfrac{4x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}$ is given by\n\n$$\nQ = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\dfrac{4x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}  \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\rho(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ \\rho(r \\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta) \\:  r \\ \\mathrm d r \\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nThe following equations connect Cartesian and polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the curve $x^2+y^2=9$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =9 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =9 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r, \\theta),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\Big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 3, \\: \\pi \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2} \\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta [{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r]\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\frac{9}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =18{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =18[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =18[-1-0] \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total charge of the quarter-disk is $Q = - 18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186412249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186412250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing Mass or Charge Over a Type I or Type II Region" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186129027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129208 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0026a41c-1953-55c7-8abe-d387671576c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129209 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129209 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [